    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0577" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg449"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 319.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West to Mr.
                            Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 28, 1885</date>.
                        (Received April 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note of the 18th
                    February last, and to the reply of your predecessor of the 8th January, I have
                    the honor to inform you that Earl Granville has directed me again to request
                    that some decision may be taken in the Tunstall case, which has been pending for
                    the last seven years.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE-WEST.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
